<title>UK: John Lewis UK store sales up 4.8% in latest week.</title>
<headline>John Lewis UK store sales up 4.8% in latest week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The John Lewis Partnership said its UK department store sales rose 4.8 percent in the week to February 1, compared with the same week a year earlier.</p>
<p>In the 52 weeks to January 25, sales were up 13.5 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Total sales, including the Waitrose supermarket chain, rose 4.2 percent in the week to February 1 and were up 12.2 percent in the 52-week period to January 25.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
